  "sol": "<p>Let <span class=\"math inline\">\\(I_j\\)</span> be the indicator of “face <span class=\"math inline\">\\(j\\)</span> never appears”, <span class=\"math inline\">\\(j = 1, \\dots, 4\\)</span>. All <span class=\"math inline\">\\(4^n\\)</span> sequences are equally likely, and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(3^n\\)</span> of them avoid face <span class=\"math inline\">\\(j\\)</span>, so <span class=\"math inline\">\\(E(I_j) = \\left(\\frac34\\right)^n\\)</span>. The number of unseen faces is <span class=\"math inline\">\\(I_1 + I_2 + I_3 + I_4\\)</span>, and by linearity its expectation is <span class=\"math inline\">\\(4\\left(\\frac34\\right)^n\\)</span>. It first drops below <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\frac12\\)</span> at <span class=\"math inline\">\\(n = 8\\)</span>: <span class=\"math inline\">\\(4\\left(\\frac34\\right)^7 \\approx 0.53\\)</span> and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(4\\left(\\frac34\\right)^8 \\approx 0.40\\)</span>.</p>\n<pre data-code=\"py\">def unseen(n):\n    seqs = list(product(range(1, 5), repeat=n))\n    return F(sum(4 - len(set(r)) for r in seqs), len(seqs))\n\n\nprint(unseen(2), 4 * F(3, 4) ** 2, unseen(3), 4 * F(3, 4) ** 3)\nprint([n for n in range(1, 20) if 4 * F(3, 4) ** n &lt; F(1, 2)][0], round(float(4 * F(3, 4) ** 7), 2))</pre>\n<pre data-code=\"out\">9/4 9/4 27/16 27/16\n8 0.53</pre>"
